2. The predefined CMaps
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ISO 32000-2 §9.7.5.2 names some seventy CMaps a PDF may reference without carrying them, and
states the obligation as a shall: "A PDF processor shall support Adobe-CNS1-7, Adobe-GB1-5,
Adobe-Japan1-7 and Adobe-KR-9 character collections." The clause adds that "[t]he CMap programs
that define the predefined CMaps are available through a variety of online sources." All 239 of
them, for the six character collections, are compiled into this binary. They live in data/cmaps/,
their provenance is data/cmaps/PROVENANCE.md, and the verbatim licence text is
